      "Language": "rus",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "It was established that the content of primary (acylhydroperoxide) and secondary (intermollecular \"seams\" in aminophospholipids) products of lipid peroxide oxidation in blood of patients with ischemic heart disease is increased against the background of hyperlipidemia and hypercholesterolemia. It is suggested that intensification of lipid peroxide oxidation may play a role in the pathogenesis of atherosclerosis."},
